hypotheses.statement:
As $X\longrightarrow\infty$, $$\label{eq:main}
 \sum_{\substack{N\pi\le X\\\pi\equiv1\pmod3\ \mathrm{prime}}}G(\pi)
 =\frac65c_*\frac{X^{5/6}}{\log X}
   +o\!\left(\frac{X^{5/6}}{\log X}\right).$$ The sum is over all primary primes in $\mathcal O$.

outputs.exact_statement:
As $X\longrightarrow\infty$, $$\label{eq:main}
 \sum_{\substack{N\pi\le X\\\pi\equiv1\pmod3\ \mathrm{prime}}}G(\pi)
 =\frac65c_*\frac{X^{5/6}}{\log X}
   +o\!\left(\frac{X^{5/6}}{\log X}\right).$$ The sum is over all primary primes in $\mathcal O$.

Suppose $RU\asymp X$, and let $(a_r)$ be divisor-bounded on $Nr\asymp R$. Suppose the smooth compactly supported weights $W_r$ have fixed support ratios and uniformly bounded derivatives, independently of $X$. For $T\ge2$ and every fixed $D>0$, $$\begin{aligned}
 &\int_{|t|\asymp T}\sum_{Nr\asymp R}|a_r|
       \left|\sum_uG(ru)(Nu)^{it}W_r(Nu/U)\right|\frac{dt}{T}
 \notag\\
 &\hspace{12mm}\ll_\epsilon
       X^{1/2+\epsilon}R^{3/4}T^{1/2}
       +O_D\bigl(X^{5/6}L^{C}T^{-D}\bigr),
 \label{eq:typeI-height}
\end{aligned}$$ where $C$ depends only on the coefficient bounds.

For squarefree $n$ on the envelope support and sufficiently large $X$, $$\label{eq:prime-detector}
 \boldsymbol 1_{\{n\ {\mathrm{prime}}\}}
 =\mathcal F_z(n)-
  \boldsymbol 1_{\{\Omega(n)=2\}}\mathcal F_z(n).$$ Moreover, $\mathcal F_z(n)$ is an exact sum of bounded-length distinguished prime tuples $$\label{eq:distinguished-tuples}
 \mathcal F_z(n)=
 \sum_{i\ge0}\frac1{i!}
 \sum_{n=\pi_1\cdots\pi_i h}
 \mathcal F_w(h)\prod_{j=1}^i
       (\psi_w(\pi_j)-\psi_z(\pi_j)).$$ Only boundedly many $i$ contribute, and the distinguished primes have norms in $[w,2z]$.

Let $X_0\asymp X$, and let $h_T$ be smooth, supported where $T\le |t|\le2T$, with $h_T^{(j)}(t)\ll_jT^{-j}$. Suppose $$L^{C_t}\le T\ll X^{1/6+\rho},\qquad B\ll\sqrt X,$$ and suppose that either $$\begin{aligned}
 T\ll X^{.01},&\qquad cX^{1/3}\le B,\quad c>0\text{ fixed},\tag{a}\\
 T\gg X^{.01},&\qquad X^{1/3-3\kappa}\le B.\tag{b}
\end{aligned}$$ Assume the structural hypotheses of Proposition <a href="#prop:dispersion" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:dispersion">13</a>, but impose neither roughness nor Siegel–Walfisz conditions. For every fixed $D>0$, by taking $C_t$ sufficiently large, $$\sum_{a,b}\alpha_a\beta_bG(ab)V\!\left(\frac{N(ab)}X\right)
 \int h_T(t)\left(\frac{N(ab)}{X_0}\right)^{it}\frac{dt}{T}
       \ll X^{5/6}L^{-D}.
 \label{eq:bilinear-integrated}$$

Let $1\le T\le X$, and let $V$ be a fixed smooth function supported in $(1/2,4)$, equal to one on a neighborhood of $[1,2]$. There is a smooth function $I_T$ such that $$I_T(s)=\frac1{2\pi}\int_{\mathbb R}
       \eta(t/T)\frac{1-2^{-it}}{it}e^{its}\,dt,
 \label{eq:interval-fourier}$$ where $\eta$ is a fixed smooth cutoff supported in $[-1,1]$ and equal to one near zero. For every $m>0$, $$\left|1_{[1,2]}(v)-V(v)I_T(\log v)\right|
 \ll_m \sum_{b\in\{0,\log2\}}
             (1+T|\log v-b|)^{-m}
 \label{eq:interval-boundary-error}$$ on the support of $V$, and the difference is zero outside it. If coefficients collected at each integer norm satisfy $|c_n|\ll_\epsilon X^\epsilon$ for $X/2<n<4X$, then $$\sum_n |c_n|\left|1_{[X,2X]}(n)
            -V(n/X)I_T(\log(n/X))\right|
       \ll_\epsilon X^\epsilon(1+X/T).
 \label{eq:perron-error}$$

Let $r$ be primary and squarefree, put $R=Nr$, and let $W$ have fixed compact support in $(0,\infty)$ and uniformly bounded derivatives. For fixed $\ell$, define $$\mathcal C_{r,\ell,t}(V;W)=
 \sum_{\substack{d,u\\(d,r)=1}}|d|G(ru)
       \theta_\ell(rud^3)N(ud^3)^{it}
       W\left(\frac{N(ud^3)}V\right).$$ Suppose $T\ge2$, $V\gg1$, and $R,V,T$ are bounded by fixed powers of $X$. Write $$M_{r,\ell,t}(V;W)=
 \boldsymbol1_{\ell=0}A_0\mathcal MW(5/6+it)V^{5/6+it}
                   \frac{\varphi(r)}{R^{7/6}}.$$ Then $$\int_{|t|\asymp T}
       |\mathcal C_{r,\ell,t}(V;W)-M_{r,\ell,t}(V;W)|
           \frac{dt}T
 \ll_{\ell,\epsilon}X^\epsilon\sqrt V\,R^{1/4}\sqrt T.
 \label{eq:angular-completed-height}$$
